  grid:
    input: 3x3
    output: 9x9 (Kronecker expansion)
  colors:
    exactly one non-black foreground color (any color 1-9)
    background is black (0)
  pattern:
    foreground_pixels: 3-5 cells out of 9
    black_pixels: 4-6 cells out of 9 (complement)
    both foreground and black must be present (neither all-black nor all-foreground)
  transform: |
    source_mask = (input != 0); tile_mask = (input == 0)
    output = kron(source_mask, tile_mask) * foreground_color
    Each foreground cell becomes a 3x3 block stamped with the black-cell pattern.
    Each black cell becomes an all-black 3x3 block.

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (input is tiny and unconstrained beyond having mixed fg/black)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size 3x3 (fixed).
    2. Pick a random foreground color from 1-9.
    3. Randomly assign each of the 9 cells to foreground or black,
       ensuring 3-5 foreground and 4-6 black (i.e. not all one type).
    4. Build output via Kronecker product of source_mask and tile_mask scaled by color.
```
</generation_spec>
